<title>USA: NYC $465 mln MAC bonds repriced, yields raised.</title>
<headline>NYC $465 mln MAC bonds repriced, yields raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co. said Wednesday it repriced Municipal Assistance Corporation for the City of New York's $465 million bond deal, raising yields in most maturities and lifting the top yield in 2008 to 5.05 percent from five percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>MUNICIPAL ASSISTANCE CORPORATION FOR THE CITY OF NEW YORK</p>
<p>(A PUBLIC BENEFIT CORPORATION OF THE STATE OF NEW YORK)</p>
<p>RE: $464,700,000*</p>
<p>SERIES H AND I BONDS</p>
<p>ISSUED PURSUANT TO THE 1991 GENL BOND RESOLUTION</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD. NOTE REPRICING AND COUPON CHANGES.</p>
<p>THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED.</p>
